Yes this is fine for now.

> d) Sent copies: should a sent message also land in a local maildir
>    through an Fcc, so it shows up in notmuch before the mirror pulls
>    it back from the list?

I'm open to suggestions but I think this is a yes. Ultimately we should
be able to restore the entire message status from the list data - but
storing the message will mark it as sent right away, which is an over
all lower latency process.
